 HELPERS\\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n\\nfunction emptyLaneScores(): MutableLaneScores {\\n  return Object.fromEntries(SCORER_LANES.map((lane) => [lane, []])) as unknown as MutableLaneScores;\\n}\\n\\nfunction projectionWithUsableSkillIds(projection: AdvisorProjection): AdvisorProjection {\\n  const skills = projection.skills.filter((skill) => {\\n    const skillId: unknown = skill.id;\\n    return typeof skillId === 'string' && skillId.trim().length > 0;\\n  });\\n  return skills.length === projection.skills.length\\n    ? projection\\n    : { ...projection, skills };\\n}\\n\\nexport function isAdvisorRrfFusionEnabled(): boolean {\\n  const value = process.env[ADVISOR_RRF_FUSION_FLAG]?.trim().toLowerCase();\\n  return value ? TRUE_FLAG_VALUES.has(value) : false;\\n}\\n\\nexport function isAdvisorQueryClassRoutingEnabled(): boolean {\\n  const value = process.env[ADVISOR_QUERY_CLASS_ROUTING_FLAG]?.trim().toLowerCase();\\n  return value ? TRUE_FLAG_VALUES.has(value) : false;\\n}\\n\\nexport function isAdvisorExactSemanticRerankEnabled(): boolean {\\n  const value = process.env[ADVISOR_EXACT_SEMANTIC_RERANK_FLAG]?.trim().toLowerCase();\\n  return value ? TRUE_FLAG_VALUES.has(value) : false;\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"---FILTER---\\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/scratch/briefs/wC.txt:\n  Line 35: Three tests fail: \"generated projection exactly equals JSON-derived ids union the residual allow-list and the doctor routes\", \"generates all inventory ids for both runtimes while scoring only the compatibility snapshots\" and \"preserves the Python bridge records, order, and owner normalization byte-for-byte\". Rewrite their expectations so each still guards its intent against the NEW rule: derive the expected values from the same source files the generator reads (hand rows from `scoring-compatibility.json`, plus one generated row per standalone-skill command that has no hand row), never from a hard-coded count copied from the current output. Keep every assertion that still holds. Do not edit the generator or any other file. If the test compares against a constant in `lib/scorer/projection.ts` named `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` that is now out of date, do NOT edit that file: report exactly what in it is stale.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/implementation-summary.md:\n  Line 80: | `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`, `ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, `ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Modified | Regenerated blocks. `projection.ts` also lost the unused `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES`. `skill_advisor.py` re-points hand-written references and limits the iteration-loop tiebreaker to the deep research and deep review bridges |\n\n  Line 134: | Remove the unused `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` from `projection.ts` | Nothing read it after activation moved to the deriver. The Python constants of the same name were already unused at HEAD and stay |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/scratch/logs/wB.out:\n  Line 32: - `projection.ts:97` and `112` — `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` still lists `memory:save` and `command-memory-save` (and `command-spec-kit` at :82), while the live `COMMAND_BRIDGES` is `GENERATED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` (:1298) and ships `command-speckit-save`. `npx vitest run tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts` passed 5/5, so I am not calling this a defect — but the retired ids are still printed in that frozen block.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/scratch/logs/wE.out:\n  Line 31: - the same deletion occurred in `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` (working tree lines 2374–2381), together with the rationale comment (\"The memory-save workflow is owned by system-spec-kit … so /memory:save normalizes there\").\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/scratch/logs/wC.out:\n  Line 20: `lib/scorer/projection.ts:80` `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` (as instructed, not edited). It is stale in three ways:\n\n  Line 24: After this change it has no consumer left (`rg HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` finds only its definition and the unrelated Python dict).\n\n  Line 26: Related observation, also not edited: `scripts/skill_advisor.py:2296` `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `:2387` `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` are likewise stale (retired `command-spec-kit`, `command-memory-save`, `command-prompt-improver`; owner map still maps `command-memory-save`) and unread by that module — dead data awaiting removal.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/scratch/logs/wA.out:\n  Line 6: **Re-pointed** (hand-written regions): `GRAPHLESS_INLINE_SKILL_IDS` (`memory:save` → `command-speckit-save`), `SKILL_ALIAS_GROUPS` key (retired id kept only as an alias string, matching the TS `aliases.ts` group), `PHRASE_INTENT_BOOSTERS` ×6 (`(\"memory:save\",1.0),(\"command-memory-save\",0.8)` → one `(\"command-speckit-save\",1.0)`), `INTENT_NORMALIZATION_RULES[\"memory\"]`, the memory-preservation-session boost (`(\"memory:save\",1.2),(\"command-memory-save\",0.8)` → one `(\"command-speckit-save\",1.2)`), `_apply_memory_save_file_operation_cap`, the per-name cap in `analyze_request`, plus comment/docstring fixes. **Removed**: `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` entries for `command-spec-kit`, `command-memory-save`, `command-prompt-improver`; their owner-normalization entry; and `COMMAND_BRIDGE_EXPLICIT_ALIASES` (its only entry mapped `/speckit:plan` → the dead umbrella id — `detect_explicit_command_intent` now returns the matched bridge id). The iteration-loop tiebreaker and `_command_bridge_owner` now match the family by prefix (`SPECKIT_COMMAND_BRIDGE_PREFIXES = (\"command-spec-kit-\", \"command-speckit-\")`). Left alone deliberately: `/memory:save` / `memory:save` as **user-typed** text (docstring example, two regexes, the `/memory:save` owner fallback).\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/spec.md:\n  Line 114: $ rg -n 'HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests\n\n  Line 115: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py:2304:HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES = {\n\n  Line 116: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/skill_advisor.py:2374:HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION = {\n\n  Line 267: | REQ-011 | `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` are deleted from the Python scorer. `CommandBridgeProjection.routingEnabled` is required and `scoringCommandBridges` keeps rows with `routingEnabled === true`. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md:\n  Line 83: - [ ] T009 [P] Delete the `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES